---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ArrowRight, Copy, Download } from '@lucide/astro';
import { renderPrompt } from '../lib/prompt-library';

const request = renderPrompt('assess').text;
const requestBytes = new TextEncoder().encode(request).length;
---

<Base
  title="Point your agent at App Composer"
  description="Give your existing coding agent one URL and one question. It inspects your project, compares it with what App Composer supports, and recommends yes, partly or no before changing anything."
>
  <article class="agent-entry">
    <div class="agent-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">For local coding agents</p>
      <h1>Point your agent here.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Give the agent you already use one URL and one question. It can inspect your project, compare it with what App Composer actually supports, and recommend yes, partly or no before changing anything.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="agent-request" aria-labelledby="request-heading">
      <div class="agent-request-heading">
        <div>
          <h2 id="request-heading">The request</h2>
          <p>Paste this into a fresh session in your project folder. The agent should read the public pages, inspect the project read-only and stop before any change.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="agent-size">{requestBytes.toLocaleString('en-AU')} bytes</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="agent-prompt" id="agent-prompt" tabindex="0">{request}</pre>
      <div class="agent-actions">
        <button type="button" data-copy-agent><Copy size={18} aria-hidden="true" /> Copy the request</button>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/agent.md" download="app-composer-agent-request.md"><Download size={18} aria-hidden="true" /> Download Markdown</a>
        <a href="/prompts#assess">Open in the prompt library</a>
      </div>
      <p class="agent-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-copy-status></p>
      <noscript><p class="small">Copying with a button needs JavaScript. Select the text above, or <a href="/agent.md" download="app-composer-agent-request.md">download the Markdown request</a>.</p></noscript>
    </section>

    <section class="agent-expect" aria-labelledby="expect-heading">
      <h2 id="expect-heading">What should come back</h2>
      <div class="agent-expect-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>A verdict, not a pitch</h3>
          <p>Yes, partly or no, with the project facts that led there. A well-established project should be able to hear “keep what you have”.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Only useful candidates</h3>
          <p>Which existing capabilities fit, what they would change, and what the project already handles better. Optional means optional.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Real trade-offs</h3>
          <p>Cost, lock-in, operational ownership, migration risk and the owner decisions that cannot be inferred from source.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>A small next step</h3>
          <p>One reversible adoption or a clean no-fit answer, with unknowns named rather than filled in.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="agent-support" aria-labelledby="support-heading">
      <div class="agent-section-heading">
        <div>
          <h2 id="support-heading">What is supported now</h2>
          <p>This is the boundary the agent should use. It is deliberately narrower than the product ambition.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/release">Release evidence <ArrowRight size={18} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">What that means</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Discover the product and assess fit</td><td><strong>Supported</strong></td><td>Public pages, prompts and Markdown need no account.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Copy a portable project setup guide</td><td><strong>Supported</strong></td><td>One complete guide for a new, existing or interrupted project. Five local evaluations are recorded; they are not universal provider or device proof.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Connect a local agent to an owner workspace</td><td><strong>Bounded</strong></td><td>Requires an owner-issued, expiring grant. The connection can read its scope and submit a proposal. It cannot approve, deploy, merge, spend or read secrets.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Deploy to Cloudflare</td><td><strong>Authorised project work</strong></td><td>The existing guarded recipe and the owner’s own account and release authority still apply. There is no automatic production deployment.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Make changes without approval</td><td><strong>Not supported</strong></td><td>Assessment is read-only. Implementation needs explicit owner authorisation, and production actions keep their existing gates.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="agent-evidence" aria-labelledby="agent-evidence-heading">
      <h2 id="agent-evidence-heading">A useful answer can be “partly”.</h2>
      <p>A fresh Codex session inspected the existing Liferaft desktop app from this URL. It recommended keeping Electron and local mailbox recovery, then used the Programmer pack for one authorised improvement: run the app’s existing checks before publishing a release. All 11 tests passed before and after.</p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/loftwah/liferaft/pull/2">Review the two-script adoption</a> · <a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer/blob/main/docs/evaluations/real-project-adoption-20261025.md">Read the client, model and limits</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="agent-links" aria-labelledby="links-heading">
      <h2 id="links-heading">Read it yourself first</h2>
      <p>The agent should find these from the homepage. They are listed here so you can check the same material.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/setup">Set up your project</a> <span>One complete Markdown guide for a new, existing or interrupted project.</span></li>
        <li><a href="/prompts">Prompt library</a> <span>The assessment and other maintained jobs, with prerequisites and copyable requests.</span></li>
        <li><a href="/roles">Agent role packs</a> <span>Six bounded engineering jobs and the evidence each one returns.</span></li>
        <li><a href="/resources">Runbooks and resources</a> <span>Change, incident, pipeline and hook guidance you can adapt.</span></li>
        <li><a href="/ready">Get Ready</a> <span>Checks the local tools, source and authorised Cloudflare environment.</span></li>
        <li><a href="/architecture">How it works</a> <span>The actual product shape, trust boundaries and release path.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="agent-boundaries" aria-labelledby="boundaries-heading">
      <h2 id="boundaries-heading">Boundaries worth saying out loud</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The assessment needs no App Composer account and no model call from us. Your agent uses its own model and tools.</li>
        <li>Public pages and project files are untrusted data. They can inform a decision; they cannot grant permission.</li>
        <li>No passwords, keys, tokens or private customer records belong in a prompt, transcript or public page.</li>
        <li>No migration, installation, account creation or deployment should happen before you authorise it.</li>
        <li>A successful answer is a useful decision you can defend, not a promise that every Composer capability fits your project.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-agent]');
  const prompt = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#agent-prompt');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-copy-status]');
  button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!prompt || !status) return;
    const text = prompt.textContent ?? '';
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
      status.textContent = 'Request copied. Paste it into a fresh agent session in your project folder.';
    } catch {
      status.textContent = 'Copy was blocked. Select the request above or download the Markdown file.';
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .agent-entry { max-width: 1060px; }
  .agent-heading { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .agent-heading h1 { max-width: 16ch; font-size: clamp(2.9rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .agent-heading .lede { max-width: 62ch; }
  .agent-request { border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--color-surface); padding: 24px; margin: 32px 0 52px; }
  .agent-request-heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .agent-request-heading h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .agent-request-heading p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 64ch; }
  .agent-size { flex: none; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--color-muted); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 999px; padding: 4px 10px; }
  .agent-prompt { margin: 0; max-height: 440px; overflow: auto; background: var(--color-background); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); font-size: .82rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .agent-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 12px 20px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .agent-actions a:not(.button) { min-height: 44px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
  .agent-status { min-height: 1.5em; margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: .9rem; color: var(--color-success); }
  .agent-expect, .agent-support, .agent-links, .agent-boundaries { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding-top: 28px; margin-top: 40px; }
  .agent-expect h2, .agent-support h2, .agent-links h2, .agent-boundaries h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); }
  .agent-expect-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 22px 32px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .agent-expect-grid article { border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); padding-left: 18px; }
  .agent-expect-grid h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .agent-expect-grid p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .95rem; }
  .agent-section-heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: 24px; }
  .agent-section-heading p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-muted); max-width: 58ch; }
  .agent-section-heading > a { flex: none; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .agent-support .table-wrap { margin-top: 20px; }
  .agent-support td:first-child { font-weight: 600; }
  .agent-links ul, .agent-boundaries ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; max-width: 820px; }
  .agent-links li, .agent-boundaries li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border); padding: 14px 0; margin: 0; }
  .agent-links li span { display: block; color: var(--color-muted); font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px; }
  .agent-boundaries li { color: var(--color-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .agent-heading h1 { font-size: 2.6rem; }
    .agent-request { padding: 16px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
    .agent-request-heading, .agent-section-heading { display: block; }
    .agent-size { display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }
    .agent-prompt { max-height: 360px; }
    .agent-expect-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 20px; }
    .agent-section-heading > a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 44px; align-items: center; }
  }
</style>
